00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:50.410
Oh, I meant to say "bear."

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:55.520
Honestly. You can't even solve 
a problem of this level?

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:59.230
Yukipii-sensei, you seem like someone 
who enjoys studying, you know?

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:00.540
It's Yukimura.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.000
I hate studying.

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:06.760
I mean, is physics and stuff 
gonna be useful in my life?

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:09.410
Mechanics and the coefficient of friction...

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:12.070
I'm never gonna use them once 
I go out and get a job.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:15.910
Unlike my older sister, I'm an idiot.

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:18.010
Even if I try, I'm not gonna get it.

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:23.090
I'm sorry, Yukipii-sensei,

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:29.090
but hanging out with friends and boba-ing 
is a way better use of my youth, right?

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:33.570
What are you doing? That's my tapioca drink!

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:39.590
You know, when I see lazy idiots 
like you, it makes my flesh crawl.

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:42.200
You ask if physics is useful?

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:44.720
Now, listen closely!

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:48.140
You are able to hold on to 
your tapioca beverage...

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.890
because of the force of static 
friction which exists in this world!

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:54.600
<b>Friction</b>

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:54.600
<b>Friction</b>

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:54.600
<b>Normal Force</b>

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:54.600
<b>Normal Force</b>

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:54.600
<b>Gasping Force</b>

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:54.610
Without friction, you 
wouldn't be able to boba!

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:56.220
For reals?

00:13:56.230 --> 00:14:04.690
<b>Weight</b>

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:59.760
Vertical force is necessary 
to support a physical object.

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:04.280
However, I am currently only 
applying horizontal force.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:04.690
<b>Force</b>

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:13.740
<b>When there is little friction,
it will slip down.</b>

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.330
When force is applied to physical objects...

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.370
an equal force will be returned in reaction.

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:13.740
<b>Normal Force N</b>

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:13.750
As a result, the frictional 
force turns upwards.

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:17.430
It's true that when I hold on 
tight it doesn't slip and fall.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:20.420
That means that the frictional 
force is higher, right?

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:22.750
The frictional force is all hyped up!

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:27.120
And frictional force is dependent 
upon the coefficient of friction.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:32.730
It's seriously impossible to pick 
up a tapioca ball with chopsticks!

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:36.020
They're extremely jelly-like and round!

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:39.010
That's because the coefficient 
of friction is low!

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:43.690
<b>Frictional Force (Stupid Low)</b>

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:43.690
<b>Normal Force</b>

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:43.690
<b>Force from Chopsticks</b>

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:43.690
<b>Gravity</b>

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.900
Because tapioca pearls are jelly-like, 
their friction coefficient is low.

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:43.690
<b>*  Jelly Factor, or more accurately,
\h\h\h\hthe smoothness of the surface.</b>

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:45.710
That is why you cannot maintain 
a hold on them with chopsticks.

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:48.680
So a friction coefficient is like 
their jelly factor, right?!

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:50.270
And that isn't all!

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:54.010
If you remove the lid, 
the tapioca pearls will leap out.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:57.040
That is the laws of inertia and motion!

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.300
Circular motion!

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:01.790
Fluid dynamics!

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:01.790
<b>Viscosity Coefficient</b>

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.300
Gas laws!

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:04.920
<b>Torricelli's Law</b>

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:05.210
<b>Stokes' Law</b>

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:05.800
<b>Circular
Motion</b>

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:08.920
<b>Archimedes'
Principle</b>

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:08.920
<b>Dalton's Law</b>

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:11.800
<b>Combined
Gas Law</b>

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:08.230
This tapioca beverage is overflowing 
with laws of physics!

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.760
In short, physics is a tapioca drink!

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.550
Tapioca's insane!

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:17.030
Now, think about that problem from earlier.

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:18.310
Will do!

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:23.080
Take this diagram, with Tapio-kun 
standing still on slope theta,

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:25.190
and indicate the forces at work.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.530
Tapii!

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.340
Tapio-kun is so cute!

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:32.800
Gravitational force, mg, 
pulls Tapio-kun downward.

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:35.560
That force can be broken down like this.

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:46.230
Tapipipipipi!

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:39.750
Tapio-kun's gonna slip down!

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.570
Oh, wait.

00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:44.950
If it's like before, and the 
frictional force is all hyped up,

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.210
<b>Friction</b>

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:46.450
that would act as a support, right?

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:47.510
Tapii!

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:51.010
And by pressing down on the floor, 
the same amount of force will be returned.

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.230
Reaction power!

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:53.270
Reaction force.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:57.230
Friction and reaction force are proportional 
to the friction coefficient.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.610
O-Oh, I get it.

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:01.970
So, it'd be like this, right?

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:01.980
Bummed

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.100
Tapi
tapii!

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.100
Vertical reaction power
- reasons

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.100
Friccction

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.100
Hyped

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:03.090
Don't get overexcited!

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:05.350
But that is correct.

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:09.110
Yay! I'm a genius, right?

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.100
Why such a huge reaction for 
a problem of this caliber?

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:13.750
Well, I mean, I'm an idiot, right?

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:16.940
And I felt like physics 
was totally impossible...

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:19.430
so understanding even a little 
makes me really happy!

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:20.990
I'm super-hyped!

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:23.340
Plus, you used tapioca as an example.

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:24.880
It's so awesome!

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:30.960
Okay! I'm gonna finish up all the rest of 
the problems in a flash and go boba-ing!

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:34.680
Don't get carried away 
over something like this!

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.370
Listen closely.

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:39.470
"I'm not going to understand anyway."

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.610
"Unlike my older sister, I'm dumb."

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:44.440
Don't ever decide anything based 
on stupid suppositions again!

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:45.610
Understand?

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:50.430
<i>...want to walk together.</i>

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:55.430
<i>That's the only thing I 
wish for so strongly</i>

00:16:55.690 --> 00:17:00.800
<i>I'll paint it up in that wide, open sky</i>

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:02.790
Hai! Hai! Hai! Hai!

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:03.900
Okay, big finish! Ready and...

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.300
Yeah!

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:11.340
Everyone, thanks for asking for an encore!

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:14.340
Ren-san!

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:14.340
Kyaaa!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.980
Amazing! Live concerts 
are amazing, Kosuke-kun!

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:21.220
Isn't it crazy? It's insane! For real!

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:23.730
Ren-san is seriously the real deal!

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:26.710
But these things are really great.

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:29.160
This feeling of being more connected 
to her than normal is insane!

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:32.040
It's awesome even on a seven 
level evaluation curve.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:34.940
It's a very valuable opinion, so you'd 
better be taking notes, Ibarada!

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:36.110
Huh?

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:37.690
Ibarada!

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:43.910
Yes.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:46.640
At the doctor's office they said there 
wasn't anything wrong in particular,

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:48.420
and that it must be fatigue.

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:52.970
I'm sorry. We'll have to leave the 
rest to you, Professor Kaihori.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:54.060
If you'll excuse me.

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:57.850
For crying out loud. 
This is the problem with shut-ins.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:00.560
It's because she came out into a 
crowd when she's not used to it.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:04.170
And she was moving around a lot, getting 
things ready for the experiment.

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:06.560
She must be exhausted.

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:09.470
That's the kind of woman she is.

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:11.990
She's always just lounging around.

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:15.320
And even though she's physically weak, 
she'll push herself too hard in weird ways.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:17.820
She did the same thing not long ago.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:22.070
Back when Professor Ikeda was 
having trouble with the brochure,

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:24.080
she said she'd made other 
people do it, but...

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.750
She's not used to exercising, 
but she did that experiment all alone.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:30.480
Then her muscles were so 
sore she practically died.

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:34.340
I see.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:38.590
Ibarada-senpai always seems 
aloof and easygoing,

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:43.810
but she's probably working hard for 
something important when we can't see her.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:46.820
Something important, huh?

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:48.970
I'm gonna go buy a little 
something to drink.

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:55.110
Argh... My brain is crazy-tired.

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.900
Review the points you learned today.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:00.230
Go ahead and drink your tapioca 
while you're doing it.

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:02.490
What? That's too much work.

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:08.780
But you know, this might be the 
first time I've had fun studying.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:09.960
Thank you.

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:14.810
To be honest, at the beginning, 
Yukipii-sensei...

00:19:14.810 --> 00:19:19.400
you were pretty rude, and I thought you 
seemed like a stubborn, study-focused nerd...

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:20.640
What did you just say?

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:25.030
But you're a super-fun, weird teacher!

00:19:25.030 --> 00:19:26.880
You're pretty good, Yukipii!

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:30.600
If there were tons of weird 
people like you, Sensei,

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.510
then university might be fun!

00:19:33.930 --> 00:19:37.250
Then diligently devote yourself 
to your studies, Kagurano Haru.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:41.560
Universities aren't so kind that 
they'd let you in as you are now.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:47.550
Himuro?

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:51.200
Ibarada-senpai, how are you feeling?

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:53.160
What about the concert?

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:55.080
It's over.

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:58.430
And we managed to safely collect 
the data from the penlights, too.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:19:59.990
Everything is fine.

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:02.850
What about Torasuke?

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:04.930
Did he have fun?

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:06.750
Of course.

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:09.570
He said that the feeling of being more 
connected than usual was "insane."

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:12.810
And that it was "awesome even on 
a seven level evaluation curve."

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:15.550
I'm glad.

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:25.450
Hey. What's so fun about waving 
those sticks around like a monkey?

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:30.330
If I cheer her on like this, it makes 
me feel like I'm one with Ren-san!

00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:34.190
But it does feel just a tiny bit lacking.

00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:40.960
I wish there was merchandise that let me 
convey the heat of my passion to her directly!

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:44.940
Isn't there some lab out there that 
can make me something like that?

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:47.010
<i>Stop it! Stop it!</i>

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:48.940
<i>Seriously, stop that kind of stuff!</i>

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:51.540
<i>You'll start seeing her differently!</i>

00:20:56.840 --> 00:20:58.360
Well, then...

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.740
who should I take home with me today?

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:03.130
Hey, Shikijou.

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:05.420
You need to be looking for 
some good women, too.

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:08.380
I've told you. I don't pick up women.

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:13.090
It's because you're always talking like a 
loser that you can't ever get a girlfriend.

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:14.570
Just watch.

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:19.230
That girl looks good from the back, 
and I'm gonna go make her fall for me.

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:24.250
That girl... Could she be...?

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:28.260
Hey there. Want to grab a 
drink with me or something?

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:29.760
I'm sorry?

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:31.860
<i>She's...</i>

00:21:31.860 --> 00:21:33.840
<i>She's from that insane 
gang of science-types!</i>

00:21:33.840 --> 00:21:36.150
It-It-It's nothing!

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:37.020
Huh?

00:21:37.550 --> 00:21:38.580
Wait!

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:41.780
Yes? Wh-What is it?

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:45.410
Um, Kanade-san... right?

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:47.330
From Saitama U.

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:49.040
Um...

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:53.810
Oh. You presented in Okinawa... didn't you?

00:21:53.810 --> 00:21:57.270
I'm sure you'll wonder what I'm 
saying all of a sudden, but...

00:21:58.650 --> 00:22:01.660
will you... go out with me

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:02.900
What?!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Next Time

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Proof 5
Science-types Fell in Love, 
So They Tried Analyzing Their Proof of Love.

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:36.580
Next time...

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:39.720
"Science-types Fell in Love, 
So They Tried Analyzing Their Proof of Love."
